From: RustDroid <dev@rustdroid.ide>
Date: 2026-08-31
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] openssl-probe: parameterize fallback prefix via RUSTDROID_PREFIX

The vendored `openssl-probe` crate probes a fixed list of system lib
paths when looking for libssl/libcrypto. Termux's adaptation adds a
hardcoded `/data/data/com.termux/files/usr/lib` entry to that list.

For RustDroid we cannot hardcode our package name — it must remain
configurable at runtime so the same toolchain tarball can be relocated
post-install (e.g. via patchelf --set-rpath + a wrapper script that
exports RUSTDROID_PREFIX).

This patch:
  1. Adds RUSTDROID_PREFIX (env var) as the *first* probed path, before
     the static fallback list. This means the on-device prefix always
     wins when set, which is what we want.
  2. Removes the hardcoded Termux path from the static fallback list
     (if present in the vendored version we're patching).
  3. Falls back to the static list if RUSTDROID_PREFIX is unset, so
     non-Android hosts still work.

Verified: applied to rust-lang/rust@1.85.0 vendor/openssl-probe/src/lib.rs
Theoretical: actual runtime behavior under on-device cargo build — must
be validated by running `cargo build` of an openssl-dep crate on-device
with RUSTDROID_PREFIX exported.
---
 vendor/openssl-probe/src/lib.rs | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vendor/openssl-probe/src/lib.rs b/vendor/openssl-probe/src/lib.rs
--- a/vendor/openssl-probe/src/lib.rs
+++ b/vendor/openssl-probe/src/lib.rs
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 use std::path::PathBuf;
+use std::env;

 pub trait ForeignLib {
     fn probe_ssl(&self) -> Result<(PathBuf, PathBuf), Error>;
@@ -65,6 +66,16 @@
 /// Probe for the OpenSSL library in a number of standard locations.
 pub fn probe_ssl() -> Result<(PathBuf, PathBuf), Error> {
     let mut candidates = Vec::new();
+
+    // RustDroid: prepend $RUSTDROID_PREFIX/lib (if set) so the on-device
+    // toolchain prefix wins over system fallbacks. This lets the same
+    // dist tarball work for any package name without rebuilding.
+    if let Ok(prefix) = env::var("RUSTDROID_PREFIX") {
+        let p = PathBuf::from(prefix).join("lib");
+        candidates.push(p.clone());
+        candidates.push(p.join("openssl"));
+    }
+
     candidates.extend(EXPLICIT_OPENSSL_LIB_DIRS.iter().cloned());

     // ... existing probe logic follows below
